    payloadLength := mload(add(data, i))
}
```

#### Analysis
The overall length check `if (dataLength < DEFAULT_DATA_LENGTH)` will ensure that the first 36 bytes (address + value + payload length) are present but it doesn't safeguard the byte reads beyond this point if `payloadLength` exceeds the remaining data available (leading to reading undefined memory areas).

##### Suggestion:
After extracting each parameter, validate that there is sufficient data left to read the next parameter or payload.

#### Example Code Fix:
```solidity
if (dataLength < DEFAULT_DATA_LENGTH) {
    revert IncorrectDataLength(DEFAULT_DATA_LENGTH, dataLength);
}
for (uint256 i = 0; i < dataLength;) {
    if (dataLength - i < 36) revert IncorrectDataLength(36, dataLength - i);
    address target;
    uint96 value;
    uint32 payloadLength;
