### Step 3: Dockerize and Deploy

#### Docker Compose
```yaml
# docker-compose.yml
version: '3'
services:
  frontend:
    build: ./frontend
    ports:
      - "3000:3000"
  backend:
    build: ./backend
    ports:
      - "4500:4500"
      - "7000:7000"
  nginx:
    build: ./nginx
    ports:
      - "80:80"
    depends_on:
      - frontend
      - backend
```

#### Nginx
```nginx
# nginx/nginx.conf
server {
  listen 80;
  server_name my-todo-app.com;

  location / {
    proxy_pass http://frontend:3000;
    proxy_set_header Host $host;
    proxy_set_header X-Real-IP $remote_addr;
    proxy_set_header X-Forwarded-For $proxy_add_x_forwarded_for;
    proxy_set_header X-Forwarded-Proto $scheme;
  }

  location /api/ {
    proxy_pass http://backend:4500;
    proxy_set_header Host $host;
    proxy_set_header X-Real-IP $remote_addr;
    proxy_set_header X-Forwarded-For $proxy_add_x_forwarded_for;
    proxy_set_header X-Forwarded-Proto $scheme;
  }
}
```

#### Dockerfiles
```dockerfile
# frontend/Dockerfile
FROM node:14

WORKDIR /app
COPY package*.json ./
RUN npm install

COPY . .
EXPOSE 3000
CMD ["npm", "start"]

# backend/Dockerfile
FROM node:14

WORKDIR /app
COPY package*.json ./
RUN npm install

COPY . .
EXPOSE 4500
EXPOSE 7000
CMD ["node", "server.js"]

# nginx/Dockerfile
FROM nginx:alpine
COPY nginx.conf /etc/nginx/nginx.conf
```

### Run and Deploy

```sh
docker-compose up --build
```

This setup will start the frontend on port 3000, backend on ports 4500 and 7000, and serve everything through nginx on port 80. You can access the application by navigating to `http://localhost/`. The backend is accessible via ports 4500 and 7000, enabling the frontend to interact with the backend's API endpoints.

### Summary
This multi-step guide walked through the creation and deployment of a TODO application with a simple but sophisticated tech stack. The design includes a neumorphism style, ensuring the app is responsive and functional on specified ports. Feel free to customize and expand upon this basic setup as needed!

