You are reading the file character by character and comparing this character to a string. In C, strings are represented as arrays of characters ending in `'\0'`. Therefore you should compare your character `ch` to a character not a string.

Instead of `ch != "\n"`, you should use `ch != '\n'`, 

```c
do {
    ch = fgetc(file);
    printf("%c", ch);
} while (ch != '\n');
fclose(file);
```
Also note that, it will exit the loop as soon as it encounters a new line character (`'\n'`). If your file has more than one line, the rest of the lines till EOF will not be read. For reading the complete file, you should still use `ch != EOF`.

