  left:0;
  right:0;
  background-color:rgba(0,0,0,0.7);
  color:#fff;
  padding:10px;
  font-size:18px;
  text-align:center;
}
```

JavaScript for slider captions:

```
var slider = document.getElementById('slider');
var sliderImages = slider.querySelector('.slider-images');
var items = sliderImages.querySelectorAll('.slider-item');
var prevButton = slider.querySelector('#slider-prev');
var nextButton = slider.querySelector('#slider-next');
var currentImage = 0;

function showImage(index) {
  var prevImage = items[currentImage];
  var nextImage = items[index];
  prevImage.classList.remove('active');
  nextImage.classList.add('active');
  currentImage = index;
}

prevButton.addEventListener('click', function() {
  var index = currentImage - 1;
  if(index < 0) {
    index = items.length - 1;
  }
  showImage(index);
});

nextButton.addEventListener('click', function() {
  var index = currentImage + 1;
  if(index >= items.length) {
    index = 0;
  }
  showImage(index);
});

showImage(currentImage);
```

In this example, we wrapped the images and captions in a `slider-item` div to position them relatively. We then added a `slider-caption` div inside each `slider-item` div that contains the caption text for the corresponding image. In the CSS, we set the position of the `slider-caption` div to the bottom of each `slider-item` div and added some styling to make it stand out.

In the JavaScript, we modified the `showImage` function to show the caption corresponding to the image when it is displayed in the slideshow. We added a `currentImage` variable to keep track of the current image index, and updated it when the user navigates through the images using the navigation buttons. When `showImage` is called with a new index, we first hide the currently displayed image by removing the `active` class from its `slider-item` div, and then display the new image by adding the `active` class to its `slider-item` div along with its corresponding caption. We also modified the `prevButton` and `nextButton` event listeners to call `showImage` with the appropriate index.

You can customize the style of the captions and their position in the slider by modifying the CSS.

